## 2. The thesis, the problem, the four pillars

### The problem

Engineers and the agents that assist them **plan in their heads and execute linearly**.
Today's coding agents (Copilot Workspace, Cursor agent, Devin, Claude Code) produce a *linear*
plan and then build. There is no shared, operable artifact that:

1. Shows the **dependency structure** of a change and which parts are **independent** (and
   therefore safely parallelizable),
2. Carries **grounded engineering analysis** per unit of work,
3. Lets a team **fan work out to multiple agents or people** without merge conflicts, and
4. Adapts its **presentation** to the size and *kind* of work.

Trellis is that artifact.

### The four pillars

| Pillar | Name | What it means | Where it lives in code |
|--------|------|---------------|------------------------|
| **P1** | **Plan Graph (DAG)** | Decompose intent into a dependency graph of grounded change-nodes; mark independent branches. | `apps/workers` planner + `engine/dependency.ts`; `packages/shared` entities |
| **P2** | **Grounded Analysis** | Every claim (assumption, risk, benefit) cites a real `file#symbol` or is labeled low-confidence. | `apps/workers/src/agents/analysis.ts`; `services/analysis` |
| **P3** | **Parallel Execution & Delegation** | Run proven-independent branches concurrently on isolated worktrees; reconverge at integration nodes; delegate subtrees. | `apps/workers/src/workers/{node-run,integration}.ts`, `runners/`, `worktree.ts`; `apps/api` delegations |
| **P4** | **Context-Adaptive Generative UI** | The canvas layout adapts to *granularity*; each node body adapts to *change type*. Always from validated specs, never raw model HTML. | `apps/web` canvas/inspector/widgets; `packages/shared/genui.ts` |

### The governing principle

> **LLMs *propose and explain*; deterministic services *enumerate and decide*.**
> The model never has the last word on a dependency.

The planner (LLM) *proposes* coarse predicted touch-sets. The **dependency engine** (pure
code) + the **Python analysis service** (tree-sitter + networkx) *decide* the real edges,
overlap, and independence. This is the safety core of the whole product.

