## 3. The six-step product spine

Every use case is an instance of this spine (`plan/00-overview/scope.md §2`):

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  D[Describe<br/>connect repo + state intent] --> P[Plan<br/>planner → nodes;<br/>engine → edges & branches]
  P --> I[Inspect<br/>5 sections + change-type widget]
  I --> It[Iterate<br/>add context → live re-plan<br/>new revision]
  It --> O[Operate<br/>run node / branch / selection<br/>parallel on worktrees]
  O --> De[Delegate<br/>prune subtree → portable spec<br/>share with role]
  It -.re-flow.-> P
  O -.drift re-derive.-> P
```

1. **Describe** — connect a repo, state intent at any granularity.
2. **Plan** — the **Planner** decomposes into Nodes; the **Dependency-Inference Engine** grounds
   each node in real symbols, derives Edges, partitions independent **Branches**.
3. **Inspect** — open a node: *Changes*, *Assumptions*, *Analysis (risks)*, *Benefits*,
   *Notable symbols*, plus a change-type widget.
4. **Iterate** — add context; the plan re-flows live (nodes/edges update, independence
   re-derived), producing a new **revision**.
5. **Operate** — Run a node / branch / selection; agents execute on isolated worktrees; diffs
   stream back; **Integration** nodes reconverge branches.
6. **Delegate** — export a subtree as a portable spec; share read-only / runnable / full
   handoff with another user or agent.

