## 7. Success metrics (FIR and friends)

**North star:** *parallel-merge-clean throughput* — plan-nodes dispatched in parallel on
proven-independent branches that merge cleanly on first integration, per active project per week.

The single most important number is **FIR**:

| KPI | Definition | Target |
|-----|------------|--------|
| **False-Independence Rate (FIR)** ⭐ | Fraction of branch-pairs marked `independent` that actually conflict on real parallel execution | **≤ 1%** (v1); ≤ 0.3% (stretch) |
| **Dependency precision** | Of asserted edges, fraction that are real | **≥ 0.92** |
| **Dependency recall** | Of real dependencies, fraction found (recall favored — a missed edge = corrupt merge) | **≥ 0.95** |
| **Parallel-merge-clean rate** | Parallel branches that integrate green, no human conflict resolution | **≥ 95%** |
| **Drift-caught-before-merge** | Build-discovered new deps re-derived before a corrupt merge | **≥ 99%** |
| **Parallel speedup (G3)** | Sequential wall-clock ÷ parallel wall-clock | **≥ 2.5×** median |
| **Analysis thumbs-up rate** | Up-votes ÷ total votes on annotation claims | **≥ 80%** |
| **Grounding rate** | Claims carrying a valid resolvable citation | **≥ 95%** |
| **Hallucination rate** | Claims citing a non-existent/wrong symbol | **≤ 2%** |
| **Time-to-first-plan (G2)** | Describe → first rendered plan | **< 30s** |
| **Incremental re-plan latency (G2)** | Add-context → re-flowed plan | **< 8s** |

Per-tier cost budgets (plan+analysis / full run incl. build): G1 ≤ $0.15/$0.50, G2 ≤
$0.75/$3, G3 ≤ $4/$20, G4 ≤ $15/$100 (guard-capped). Instrumentation intent: **PostHog**
(product + LLM cost), **OpenTelemetry** (latency / parallel-vs-sequential), and the **eval
harness** (golden-repo CI gates). *(Instrumentation is planned; not yet wired in the as-built
code.)*

