## 8. System architecture

Trellis is a **pnpm monorepo** of four runtime services plus two shared packages, over
**Supabase Postgres** (durable truth) and **Redis** (ephemeral control plane).

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph Client
    CC["Claude Code<br/>/trellis slash cmd"]
    Web["apps/web<br/>Next.js canvas (React Flow)"]
  end

  subgraph ControlPlane["apps/api — Fastify /v1 + MCP (stdio)"]
    API["REST routes + services<br/>validate → persist → enqueue → return"]
    MCP["MCP server<br/>trellis_plan / get_plan / status / run_branch"]
  end

  subgraph Workers["apps/workers — BullMQ (one process, 4 workers)"]
    PB["plan-build"]
    AN["analysis"]
    NR["node-run"]
    IN["integration"]
  end

  subgraph Analysis["services/analysis — Python FastAPI"]
    PY["tree-sitter + networkx<br/>/index /resolve-touchset /overlap /callgraph-impact"]
  end

  Redis[("Redis<br/>BullMQ queues · locks · run streams")]
  Supa[("Supabase<br/>Postgres + Auth + Realtime + Storage")]
  Anthropic["Anthropic API<br/>Opus 4.8 / Sonnet 4.6"]
  Repo["Git repo<br/>ephemeral worktrees"]

  CC -->|MCP stdio| MCP
  Web -->|HTTPS /v1| API
  Web <-->|Realtime| Supa
  Web -->|SSE run stream| API
  API --> Redis
  API --> Supa
  MCP --> API
  Redis <--> Workers
  Workers --> Supa
  Workers --> PY
  Workers --> Anthropic
  Workers --> Repo
  PY --> Redis
```

**Boot philosophy of the API:** *validate → persist (service-role Supabase) → enqueue (BullMQ)
→ return*. Long agent work runs in the separate workers process and streams back over a Redis
Stream (SSE to the canvas) and Supabase Realtime (durable graph changes).

**Durable vs ephemeral split (ADR-2):** Supabase = truth (plans, nodes, edges, branches,
runs, annotations, delegations…); Redis = control plane (queues, distributed locks, live run
log streams, presence, symbol-graph cache).

