## 10. Monorepo layout (file-by-file)

```
google-genui/
├── apps/
│   ├── web/        Next.js generative-UI canvas
│   ├── api/        Fastify orchestration REST API (/v1) + MCP launcher
│   └── workers/    BullMQ workers: planner, analysis, node-run, integration
├── packages/
│   ├── shared/     @trellis/shared — zod schemas + TS types (the contracts)
│   └── db/         @trellis/db — Postgres schema/migrations + admin client
├── services/
│   └── analysis/   Python FastAPI dependency-analysis service
├── plan/           Canonical product/architecture design docs (728 KB)
├── docker-compose.yml   Redis 7 (Supabase runs separately via CLI)
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml  workspaces: apps/* + packages/*
├── tsconfig.base.json   shared TS config + path aliases
├── .env.example         documented env template (the only tracked env file)
└── README.md            build quickstart
```

> **As-built note:** `plan/05-implementation/repo-structure.md` envisioned extra packages
> (`ui`, `agent-core`, `git-worktree`). In the real repo those are folded into `apps/web`
> (design system in `lib/` + `components/ui/`) and `apps/workers` (`runners/`, `worktree.ts`).
> Only `packages/shared` and `packages/db` exist as standalone packages.

### `apps/api/src/` — Fastify orchestration API (`@trellis/api`)

| File | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `index.ts` | `buildServer()` factory; CORS; global error + not-found handlers; registers all routes under prefix `/v1`; `start()` listens on `API_PORT` (default 8080); graceful shutdown closes queues. Auto-starts only when run directly (robust `fileURLToPath` main-module check). |
| `env.ts` | Centralized env accessor; `DEV_IDENTITY` constant; lazy-required secrets. |
| `auth.ts` | `authPreHandler` — verifies Supabase JWT (HS256 via `jose`), attaches `request.identity = {userId, orgId, email}`; dev bypass when `NODE_ENV=development` and no token. |
