| `integration_nodes` | Reconvergence: `plan_id, target_branches uuid[], status, conflict_report jsonb, merge_commit`. |
| `delegations` | Subtree handoff: `plan_id, subtree_root_node, spec_path, assigned_to_user, assigned_to_email, role (runner), status (draft), base_commit, created_by`. |
| `shares` | Access grant: `resource_type (plan|project), resource_id, principal_user, principal_email, role, created_by`. |
| `comments` | Node discussion: `node_id, author, body, resolved`. |
| `events` | Append-only audit + realtime fan-out: `plan_id, actor, type, payload jsonb`. |
| `feedback` | P2 trust loop: `node_id, annotation_path, vote (up|down), reason, "user"`. |

Indexes: `plan_nodes(plan_id,revision)`, `plan_edges(plan_id,revision)`, `runs(plan_id,status)`,
`branches(plan_id)`, `delegations(plan_id,status)`, `events(plan_id,created_at)`.

### Row-Level Security (defined, but bypassed by the service-role workers/api)

RLS is **default-deny**; the migration defines helpers `auth_org()`, `role_rank()`, and
`can_access_plan(plan, min_role)` which grants access when the caller is in the plan's org, OR
has a `shares` grant ≥ min_role, OR has a `delegations` grant ≥ min_role. Policies: read =
viewer, write = editor, run-insert = runner; child tables inherit from their parent plan.

> **Important as-built nuance:** the API and workers use the **service-role** key, which
> **bypasses RLS**. Authorization is therefore enforced in the **services layer** by scoping
> every query to `identity.orgId` (and plan/project ids). Out-of-org access returns **404**
> (not 403) to avoid leaking resource existence. RLS is the second line of defense for any
> direct (anon-key) access — e.g. the browser's Supabase Realtime subscriptions.

