## 12. Shared contracts (`@trellis/shared`)

`packages/shared/src/index.ts` re-exports everything. These zod schemas are the **single
contract** across api ↔ workers ↔ web, and they mirror the Postgres enums and the Python
pydantic models.

### `entities.ts` — domain objects

- **`TouchSet`** — `{ predicted:{add,modify,delete: SymbolRef[]}, resolved?:{files, symbols,
  signatures_changed, schema_keys, config_keys}, resolution_confidence? }`. `SymbolRef =
  {kind, name, file?}`. The substrate of all dependency reasoning.
- **`Project`, `Plan`, `PlanNode`, `PlanEdge`, `Branch`, `Run`, `Delegation`, `Share`** — match
  the tables above.
- **`EdgeEvidence`** — `{reason: symbol_dependency|file_overlap|data_flow|signature_change|
  schema_dependency|sequence, shared[], from_provides[], to_consumes[], overlap_score}`.
- **`NodeAnnotation`** — the five inspector sections:
  - `assumptions[]` = `{text, grounded_refs[], confidence}`
  - `analysis[]` (risk register) = `{kind: race_condition|failure_mode|edge_case|perf|security,
    text, grounded_refs[], severity: low|medium|high, confidence}`
  - `benefits[]` = `{text, grounded_refs[]}`
  - `notable_symbols[]` = `{symbol, file, role, why_notable}`
  - `widget_specs[]` = `WidgetSpec[]`
- **`PlanGraph`** = `{plan, nodes[], edges[], branches[], annotations[]}` — the canonical
  payload `GET /v1/plans/:id` returns and the canvas renders.

### `genui.ts` — generative-UI contracts

- **`CanvasKind`** = `checklist | compact_dag | swimlane_dag | hierarchical_map` (G1→G4).
- **`LayoutSpec`** = `{tier, canvas, direction (LR|TB), grouping (by_module|by_milestone|null),
  emphasis[], parallelism_ui (hidden|branch_buttons|dispatch_parallel|assign_clusters),
  delegation_ui (share_diff|per_branch|per_lane|assign_clusters), semantic_zoom,
  default_inspector_tab (changes|contract|assumptions|analysis)}`. The planner emits one per plan.
- **`WidgetKind`** = MVP: `schema_diff, api_contract, component_preview, call_graph_impact`;
  phase-2: `key_diff, test_linkage, resource_diagram, markdown, checklist`.
- **`WidgetSpec`** = `{widget, version, props (record), grounding[], fallback_text?}`. The
  analysis agent emits these per node; the client validates them at the registry boundary
  before rendering (never raw model HTML).

### `api.ts` — REST DTOs

`CreatePlanRequest`, `ReplanRequest`, `RunSelectionRequest`, `DelegateRequest`,
`ShareRequest`, `ApiError`. The API validates inbound bodies against these.

### `runner.ts` — the execution contract

- **`WorkOrder`** — what a runner receives: `{run_id, node_id, plan_id, revision, base_commit,
  worktree_path, goal, touch_set:{allowed_files, allowed_symbols, signatures}, assumptions[],
  risks[], acceptance:{tests[],commands[]}, policy:{network, fs_scope:"worktree", max_turns,
  wallclock_s}}`. The `touch_set` is the **guardrail** from the dependency engine.
- **`RunnerResult`** — `{run_id, status, files_touched[], drift[], diff_artifact, tokens, cost,
  summary}`.
- **`RunnerEvent`** — `{type: text|tool_call|file_edit|token_usage|error|status, at, data}`.
- **`AgentRunner`** interface — `{id, start(order, io), cancel(runId)}`. Claude Code is the v1
  runner; native is the fallback. **Orchestration owns safety** (worktree isolation, drift
  audit, test gate); the runner only writes code in the worktree.

### `keys.ts` — Redis keys & queue names

- **`QUEUES`** = `{planBuild:"plan-build", nodeRun:"node-run", analysis:"analysis-jobs",
  integration:"integration", replan:"replan"}`. ⚠️ Note the analysis queue's literal name is
  **`analysis-jobs`**. (BullMQ names must not contain `:`.)
- **`keys`** = `symbolGraph`, `touchSet`, `lockPlan`, `lockBranch`, `lockNode`, `lockFile`,
  `runStream(runId)="stream:run:{id}"`, `presence`.

