## 14. The workers (`apps/workers`)

One Node process boots **all four BullMQ workers** ("the BRAIN"). Concurrency: plan-build **2**,
analysis **4**, node-run **`MAX_CONCURRENT_BRANCHES`** (default 4), integration **1**. Workers
generally **do not rethrow** on LLM/schema failures (they mark the row failed + record an
event) to avoid BullMQ retry-storms.

### Worker: `plan-build` (queue `plan-build`)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant API
  participant Q as BullMQ
  participant W as plan-build worker
  participant Repo as Git/worktree
  participant PY as Analysis service
  participant AI as Anthropic (Opus)
  participant DB as Supabase

  API->>Q: enqueue plan-build {plan_id}
  Q->>W: job
  W->>DB: plans.status = planning; insert plan run (running)
  W->>Repo: ensureRepo() (clone or sample)
  W->>PY: POST /index (best-effort)
  W->>W: buildRepoSummary()
  W->>AI: runPlanner() → emit_plan (nodes + LayoutSpec)
  loop per node
    W->>PY: resolveNode() /resolve-touchset (or TS fallback)
  end
  W->>W: deriveDependencies() (edges + branches + independence)
  W->>DB: insert branches → plan_nodes → plan_edges; status = ready; layout_spec
  W->>DB: recordEvent(plan.ready)
  loop per node
    W->>Q: enqueue analysis-jobs {node_id}
  end
```

### Worker: `analysis` (queue `analysis-jobs`)

For each node: loads the node + plan, runs the analysis agent (Opus, `emit_annotations`),
**upserts `node_annotations`** (1:1 on `node_id`) with the five sections + widget specs +
model/tokens, records `node.annotated`. Best-effort — never blocks plan readiness or execution.

### Worker: `node-run` (queue `node-run`)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant W as node-run worker
  participant DB as Supabase
  participant Repo as Git
  participant R as Runner (Claude Code)
  participant S as Redis stream

  W->>DB: load node (skip if built/merged); load plan/project/annotations
  W->>DB: insert run (node_build, running); node.status = running
  W->>Repo: ensureRepo() → createWorktree() off base_commit
  W->>DB: node.worktree_ref = wt.ref
  W->>W: build WorkOrder (touch_set guardrail, assumptions, risks, acceptance)
  W->>R: getRunner(backend).start(order)
  R-->>S: stream events (text/tool_call/file_edit/status)
  R-->>W: RunnerResult
  W->>Repo: diffWorktree() + changedFiles()
  W->>W: drift = touched files outside allowed_files
  alt drift detected
    W->>DB: recordEvent(node.drift); stream status:drift
  end
  W->>DB: node.status = built|blocked|failed; update run (tokens/cost/result)
  W->>Repo: worktree.remove()  (GC)
```

Backend precedence: `job.execution_backend ?? project.execution_backend ?? env.executionBackend`.

### Worker: `integration` (queue `integration`)

Takes a **plan lock** (`SET lock:plan:{id} … NX`, 600s). Resolves target branches (explicit or
all `built`). Creates a fresh integration worktree off base_commit, then **sequential
`git merge --no-ff`** of each branch's built-node worktrees:

- **First textual conflict** → `git merge --abort`; write `conflict_report` (kind `textual`);
  branch `conflicted`; `plans.status = partially_merged`; **stop** (no auto-merge on red).
- All clean → **test gate** (`detectTestCommand`, 5-min kill). Red gate → `conflict_report`
  (kind `semantic`); `partially_merged`; stop. No test command → treated green (MVP).
- Green → commit; `integration_nodes.status = merged` + `merge_commit`; branches `merged`;
  built nodes `merged`; `plans.status = merged`; record `integration.merged`.

Releases the lock only if the token still matches (compare-and-del).

