## 17. The agent system (models, prompts, tool-forced JSON)

| Agent | Job | Model | Tool |
|-------|-----|-------|------|
| **Planner** | `prompt + repo summary` → `Nodes[]` (change_type, summary, coarse predicted touch_set) + `LayoutSpec` | **Opus 4.8** | `emit_plan` |
| **Dependency engine** | *(deterministic, not an LLM)* resolve → edges → branches → independence | — | — |
| **Analysis / annotation** | per node → 5 sections + `WidgetSpec[]`, every claim grounded | **Opus 4.8** | `emit_annotations` |
| **Builder** | execute one node on an isolated worktree → diff/tests/tokens/cost | **Sonnet 4.6** (via Claude Code) | — |
| **Integration** | merge reconverging branches + test gate | (deterministic git + test) | — |
| **Replan / drift** | re-derive the plan on new context or build drift → new revision | **Opus 4.8** | *(planned; `replan` queue has no worker yet)* |

### The core primitive: `toolForcedJSON<T>()`

Every LLM agent uses exactly one forced terminal tool (`emit_*`):
`client.messages.create({model, tools:[{name, input_schema}], tool_choice:{type:"tool",
name}})`. The result is **zod-validated**; on a missing tool-call or validation failure it does
**bounded repair** (≤2 retries) quoting the exact validator error back to the model, then throws
if exhausted. This is how the system gets reliable structured output from the models.

### Grounding enforcement (P2)

The analysis agent is told to **ground every claim** (≥1 `grounded_refs` to a real `file#symbol`
in the touch-set/blast-radius, else confidence < 0.5). After the call, TS code **re-checks**:
any assumption/risk with confidence ≥ 0.5 but unresolved refs is **demoted to 0.4**. Grounded
high-severity risks are never silenced. A default widget is injected if the model emits none
(keyed by `change_type` via `WIDGET_FOR_CHANGE_TYPE`).

