## 24. The "degrade-never-crash" philosophy

A pervasive, symmetric design choice: every external dependency has a graceful fallback so a
demo/dev run always completes.

| If this is missing/unavailable… | …the system does this instead |
|---------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| Repo URL / clone fails | generates a tiny committed **sample repo** |
| Python analysis service down | TS-side heuristics: predicted-as-resolved @ confidence 0.4; **Jaccard** file overlap |
| Claude Code binary missing / spawn fails | falls back to the **NativeRunner** stub |
| tree-sitter grammar missing / file unparseable | file skipped + counted (`skipped_files`); never crashes |
| Redis (analysis cache) absent | in-memory cache only |
| API / Supabase unconfigured (web) | every hook + PromptBox fall back to bundled **fixtures** (all four layouts + every widget render) |
| LLM/schema failure in a worker | mark row failed + record event; **do not rethrow** (no BullMQ retry-storm) |

